No more than one interface is allowed for a  node,  and  no  more
than  one  IPv6  interface  address  is allowed for an interface.
This is to avoid source address selection conflicts  between  the
IPv6 layer and the IPv4 layer, and to cope with ingress filtering
rules  on  the  other side.  This is a feature to make work right
for all occasions.
